// Pull request: #6195 Add rule: HackTool - Kerbrute Execution
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6195
// Pull request author: ashish-cybersec
// Change: new rule
// Title: HackTool - Kerbrute Execution
// Sigma ID: 65584b02-bc8b-49e0-bea2-2977b48999b5
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Ashish Pulivarthy (ashish-cybersec)
// Date: 2026-07-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1110, discovery, T1087.002
// Description: Detects the execution of Kerbrute, a tool used to enumerate valid Active Directory accounts and
//   to brute-force or spray passwords via Kerberos Pre-Authentication. Its "userenum" mode
//   enumerates valid domain usernames without generating failed logon events (Event ID 4625), making
//   it a stealthy discovery technique, while its "passwordspray", "bruteuser" and "bruteforce" modes
//   increment failed login counters and can lock out accounts.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/ropnop/kerbrute
//   - https://www.securonix.com/blog/hunting-kerbrute-analysis-detection-and-mitigation-of-kerberos-attacks-in-active-directory/
//   - https://raxis.com/blog/cool-tools-series-kerbrute/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ff3e54c326ffb63826deb75d7dc57e0a9cb7f25d/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_kerbrute.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\kerbrute.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\kerbrute_windows_386.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\kerbrute_windows_amd64.exe") or ((ProcessCommandLine contains " bruteforce " or ProcessCommandLine contains " bruteuser " or ProcessCommandLine contains " passwordspray " or ProcessCommandLine contains " userenum ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " --dc " or ProcessCommandLine contains " --domain " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -d "))
